<title>HONG KONG: Cathay welcomes runway go ahead.</title>
<headline>Cathay welcomes runway go ahead.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cathay Pacific Airways Limited said it welcomed the go- ahead for a second runway at Manchester airport.</p>
<p>&quot;Although Cathay is not looking to increase frequency into Manchester in the near future, a second runway will give us the chance to optimise arrival and departure timings in the medium term,&quot; a Cathay spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Cathay currently has daily flights to the north west of England airport via Amsterdam, Frankfurt or Paris. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
